{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>In one house it shall be eaten.</b> In one חֲבוּרָה — that those registered for it should not form two חֲבוּרוֹת and divide it. Would you say in one חֲבוּרָה, or does it mean only in one house, literally — and to teach that if they began and were eating in the courtyard and rain came down, they may not go inside the house? Scripture says: ״עַל הַבָּתִּים אֲשֶׁר יֹאכְלוּ אֹתוֹ בָהֶם״ — from here, that the one eating may eat in two places." "<b>You shall not take out of the house.</b> Out of the חֲבוּרָה." "<b>And a bone you shall not break in it.</b> One fit for eating — for instance, if it has on it a k'zayit of meat — there is in it the prohibition of breaking a bone; if it does not have on it a k'zayit of meat, there is not in it the prohibition of breaking a bone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:52.963068239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}